  "upload": {
    "title": "Coca-Cola's Recipe Is Locked in a Vault 🔒 #shorts",
    "description": "Coca-Cola's secret formula sits in a vault at the World of Coca-Cola in Atlanta; it was moved there in December 2011 from a SunTrust bank vault, where it had been kept since 1925. Popular legend says only two executives know the full formula and never travel together. Coke never patented the recipe, because a patent expires and becomes public; as a trade secret it can stay protected indefinitely. The twist: in 1979 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution printed a photo of a handwritten early recipe, and in 2011 This American Life said it had tracked down the original. Coca-Cola says it is not the real formula.",
